                        "entry_id": "5a7979b9-0636-3905-81f5-8beb296ef459",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vélo à pignon fixe, sans roue libre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bcb3bf1c-f2ec-3861-954c-fa2587a8832e",
                        "entry_id": "5a7979b9-0636-3905-81f5-8beb296ef459",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Il reconnaît que plusieurs cyclistes enlèvent les freins sur les fixies, comme on appelle les vélos à pignon fixe. — (« Un coroner contre la vague des vélos sans freins », Le Devoir.com, 10 juin 2013)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6307263c-3795-3da1-aba8-2d986c3ee3ca",
                        "entry_id": "5a7979b9-0636-3905-81f5-8beb296ef459",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Le fixie est une remise au goût du jour des premières bicyclettes, quand, au début du XXᵉ siècle, le dérailleur n’existait pas encore et que l’on n’imaginait pas poser de frein sur son deux-roues. — (Julien Jégo, « Dans les roues de fans des “fixies” parisiens », Le Monde.fr, 18 octobre 2012)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "796c1056-cae8-43e8-ae06-7499e8e1a4af",
                        "source_entry_id": "5a7979b9-0636-3905-81f5-8beb296ef459",
                        "target_lang_word": "fixie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fixie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f858e66a-85db-385f-a3a0-28ea5f630e28",
                                        "entry_id": "a4114978-39ca-3892-a9a6-60cc9df5a228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fixed-gear bicycle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20232ae2-a613-45da-b24b-388818a02d26",
                                                "sense_id": "f858e66a-85db-385f-a3a0-28ea5f630e28",
                                                "text": "A number of couriers in NYC use `fixies' -- fixed-gear bikes with no brakes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e38cd93-0795-439e-8afe-fc3fe9cfbe98",
                                                "sense_id": "f858e66a-85db-385f-a3a0-28ea5f630e28",
                                                "text": "Coming from San Francisco, where gentrification swept through neighborhoods faster than hipster trends like fixies, tattoos, and retro eighties wardrobes, I didn't think Erin had anything to worry about."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ad681f2-2466-4b69-ae08-1ee269b6e1bb",
                                                "sense_id": "f858e66a-85db-385f-a3a0-28ea5f630e28",
                                                "text": "[F]ixed-gear bikes, or \"fixies,\" cycles that have one speed and are built without the free-wheel equipment that keeps a regular bicycle's pedals stationary while the tires are in motion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34cc6b97-356e-32be-a3c2-06450e189b8d",
                                        "entry_id": "a4114978-39ca-3892-a9a6-60cc9df5a228",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fixed-blade knife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b710fd54-073e-4bc8-a2c1-d88d95278a01",
                                                "sense_id": "34cc6b97-356e-32be-a3c2-06450e189b8d",
                                                "text": "Among the other fixed blades en route is the Aegis FX. As the name indicates this is a fixie version of SOG's renovated Aegis folder, which debuted at the beginning of 2020."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9601d23-cd3d-4c37-a2ad-c2fda301ef27",
                                                "sense_id": "34cc6b97-356e-32be-a3c2-06450e189b8d",
                                                "text": "In my humble opinion, a great horizontal Kydex sheath is the ONLY way to make a fixie disappear on your person."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
